  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Parc naturel départemental de la Grande Corniche covers 712 hectares between La Trinité, Villefranche-sur-Mer, Èze and La Turbie, from Mont Leuze to Mont Bataille. The park is part of the Natura 2000 site "Corniches de la Riviera" (Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office). From the Fort de la Revère, a walk overlooks the coast along the corniche and passes military architecture works, with a panoramic view over the Côte d'Azur.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park's official regulation, published by the Département (Randoxygène), requires a collar and leash year-round for dogs; category-1 dogs are banned and category-2 dogs must be muzzled. The park is reachable by car from Nice via the Route Métropolitaine de la Grande Corniche (RM 2465), heading towards La Turbie, as far as the Col d'Èze; the main car parks are at the Fort de la Revère and the Plateau de la Justice. The park is open from 7:30am to 8pm from 1 April to 31 October, and from 8am to 6pm from 1 November to 31 March (Département page, updated 29/04/2026). Dogs must also stay away from the landscaped areas (see below) and must not disturb the peace of other users or the wildlife.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: head for the Fort de la Revère for the panoramic view over the Côte d'Azur, then a break at the picnic area; keep the leash short, the park's wildlife is protected.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The park covers the territory of four communes, Èze, La Turbie, La Trinité and Villefranche-sur-Mer, which can be reached from the Col d'Èze to extend the outing.</p>
      <p>Bring your own water for your dog, especially in summer: the Département's page lists a "toilets / water point" among the park's facilities, without saying where it is, along with picnic table-benches, an orientation table, a bird-watching area, footpaths and a fitness trail.</p>
      <p><strong>Additional rules:</strong> the park regulation bans animals from play areas, educational areas, fitness areas and sports trails. The Piste de la Forna is closed to the public until further notice (Département, updated 29/04/2026); the rest of the park remains open. The park has three discovery trails and a Maison de la Nature, with a car park for people with reduced mobility nearby.</p>
      <p><strong>Getting there:</strong> park address: route de la Revère, 06360 Èze. From the A8 motorway, exit La Turbie, then departmental road 2564 to the Col d'Èze, from where the route de la Revère leaves on the right and, 500 metres further on, the route du plateau de la Justice. Car parks are at the main access points, notably at the Plateau de la Justice and the Fort de la Revère.</p>
      <p><strong>Check before you go:</strong> the state of access and trails on the Département's page on the day of your visit (the Piste de la Forna is closed "until further notice") and any restrictions on access to forest massifs during periods of wildfire risk.</p>
      <p>Sources read on 25/11/2026: <a href="https://www.departement06.fr/annuaire-general/parc-de-la-grande-corniche">Alpes-Maritimes Département (park page)</a>, <a href="https://www.departement06.fr/sites/default/files/media/downloads/dpt06-parcs-departementaux_reglement-gdecorniche.pdf">park regulation</a>, <a href="https://randoxygene.departement06.fr/parc-de-la-grande-corniche">Randoxygène</a>, <a href="https://www.explorenicecotedazur.com/nature/parc-naturel-departemental-de-la-grande-corniche">Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office</a>.</p>
